Personal Portfolio Website

A responsive personal portfolio website showcasing my skills, projects, background, and contact information as a junior fullstack developer.
Features
Responsive navigation bar with smooth section navigation
Home section introducing the developer
About section with personal and professional information
Skills section displaying technical skills
Projects section showcasing completed projects
Contact section with email and GitHub links
Responsive design for different screen sizes
Interactive elements powered by JavaScript
Clean and modern user interface
Technologies Used
HTML5 – Used to structure the website
CSS3 – Used for styling, layout, responsiveness, and visual design
JavaScript – Used to add interactivity and dynamically display content
Git – Used for version control
GitHub – Used to host the project and manage the repository
GitHub Pages – Used to deploy the website
How to Run Locally
Clone the repository:
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/portfolio-website.git
Navigate into the project folder:
cd portfolio-website
Open the project in Visual Studio Code.
Open index.html in your browser, or use the Live Server extension in VS Code to run the website locally.
What I Learned

Through this project, I learned how to structure a complete one-page website using HTML, style and make it responsive with CSS, and use JavaScript to dynamically create and manage content. I also gained practical experience using Git and GitHub for version control and deploying a website using GitHub Pages.